{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Whoever sheds a man's blood.</b> In an earthly court." "<b>For in the image of Elohim.</b> The reason human blood is required to be accounted for while the blood of other living creatures is not: because in the image of Elohim — meaning the separate substances called אֱלֹהִים (Exodus 22:8) — one of them made man. For indeed, from the time the blessed El said נַעֲשֶׂה אָדָם (Genesis 1:26), He granted power to the separate substances, or to one of them, to bestow intellectual power upon every prepared subject — that is, upon each individual of the human species. And since man is in the image of Elohim, which is his human soul whereby he lives as an intelligent being, it is fitting that his blood and his vital soul — which serve this image — should be held accountable and required at the hand of those who destroy them, more than the lives of all other living creatures."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:35.323924506Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}